,{"method":"electromagnetics","page":28,"text":"Surge Copper has a soil database for the Berg property containing 10,108 soil samples, composed of 4082 samples that have been comp"},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":29,"text":"As part of a land options deal Surge consolidated claims covering the Boundary target on the west side of the Berg claim block ."},{"method":"magnetics","page":72,"text":"and in June 2009 by Har ris and Labrenz titled \u201c2009 Mineral Berg 2017 Aeromagnetic and Geological Mapping Surveys January, 2018 Thompson Creek Metals Company Inc.","platform":"airborne"},{"method":"magnetics","page":73,"text":"of 11,659.6 metres of diamond drilling in 31 holes and a total field ground magnetic survey performed in the deposit area to determine t he geophysical characteristics of the deposit.","platform":"ground","year":2008},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":75,"text":"In 1973, an 11.3 line-km frequency domain IP survey was completed over Berg ette, extending 1,600 m to the north up Bergette Valley.","year":1973,"line_km":11.3},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":76,"text":"the Berg and Bergette areas in 2010 shows Bergette has a similar size resistivity response (Z1 -Off) as the Berg deposi t ( Figure 6-3 below).","year":2010},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":79,"text":"The first publicly recorded work is a 9.3 line -km dipole -dipole IP survey that identified four or five anomalous zones (Walker, 1974) that were followed -up with 646 m of diamond drilling o ver seven holes (Belik, 1974","year":1974},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":81,"text":"A 17.4 line -km IP survey was completed in the CS South zone to follow up on three distinct multi -element geochemical anomalies from Ah sampling completed in 2015 (Swant","year":2016,"platform":"airborne"},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":81,"text":"is coincident with an oval -shaped 1,300 m x 900 m high magnetic and electromagnetic response from a helicopter -borne survey completed in 2010 (Branson and Guestrin, 2016).","year":2010},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":82,"text":"Hudson Bay Oil and Gas Limited in 1973 (Sylvia claims) to cover a regional induced polarization anomaly situated on the flank of a prominent airborne magnetic high.","platform":"airborne","year":1973},{"method":"magnetics","page":82,"text":"Similarly, results of the IP and magnetometer surveys showed several minor anomalies but did not present any highly compelling targets for future work.","platform":"ground","year":1974},{"method":"magnetics","page":90,"text":"of the Berg deposit within a parallel N -S oriented regionally anomalous aeromagnetic trend (Jago and Pond, 2018).","platform":"airborne","year":2018},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":98,"text":"geophysical techniques ( induced polarization, airborne magnetics and resistivity) help outline the Berg deposit and show promise for discovering new zones of porphyry style mineralization that can build the resource base in","platform":"airborne"},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":101,"text":"A property wide helicopter -borne ZTEM and aeromagnetic survey was conducted over the combined Ootsa and Berg Properties by Geotech Lt d.","platform":"airborne"},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":102,"text":"carried out a helicopter -borne ZTEM and aeromagnetic survey over the Berg property and the adjacent Ootsa prop","platform":"airborne","year":2021},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":105,"text":"grab samples) and 2 ,265 soil samples, and 47.5 line km (20 lines) of DC resistivity -induced polarization geophysical surveys as illustrated in Figure 9-6 and Figure 9-7.","year":2022,"line_km":47.5},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":106,"text":"The Bergette target is hosted within a kilometre scale copper -in-soil anomaly that overlies a distinct ZTE","year":2022},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":106,"text":"The target has b een drilled previously, most notably in 1972, with encouraging results.","year":1972},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":111,"text":"shows a compilation map over the Berg -SW Berg target area with a 2007 induced polarization geophysical survey that partially covers the SW Berg target.","year":2007,"platform":"airborne"},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":115,"text":"The next steps for this target will include ground -based induced polarization surveying and drill testing if warranted.","platform":"ground"},{"method":"seismic","page":118,"text":"In addition, 20 seismic refraction geophysical survey lines were completed to map overburden thickness, depth to bedrock, and measure shear and compres sional wave veloci"},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":382,"text":"38. Hallof, P. G. and Goudie, M. A. (1973). Report on the Induced Polarization and Resistivity Survey on the Bergette Option, Tahtsa Lake Area. Omineca Mining Division, B.C. for Granges Exploration Aktiebolag.","year":1973},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":384,"text":"McCance, J. A. (1976). Report on Induced Polarization and Magnetometer Surveys; Sylvia Claims. Assessment Report 6078, Assessment Reports - Province of British Columbia (gov.bc.ca) p.","year":1976},{"method":"magnetics","page":384,"text":"(2010). Report on helicopter -borne aeroTEM system electromagnetic, magnetic survey \u2013 Berg project, Smithers, BC, Canada. Assessment Report 32307, Assessment Reports - Province of British Columbia (gov.bc.ca) p. 62.","year":2010}],"targets":[{"page":81,"explained":false,"untested":true,"text":"A compilation map of the Sibola target is shown in Figure 6-4. An IP survey over the area shows a 2 km by 2 km chargeability anomaly that is open to the south. Two prominent magnetic highs correspond with zones of high chargeability (labelled A and B in the Fi"},{"page":102,"explained":true,"untested":false,"text":"The Berg deposit is located with a large magnetic low sitting at the ce nter of circular magnetic high, likely reflecting the intrusive geometry and a hornfelsed ring surrounding the intrusion."},{"page":106,"explained":true,"untested":fa